  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14248692/assets/72462d252e84e20d567ccd10c2be12a6496f442f08d6e6baa609c5fb74f6fcc5.png)\n\n     \n\nIf we were to fold the net above along its edges, then we'd get a triangular prism, as shown below: \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14248692/assets/8e77623f767c9cea456b787a09465397a4360915c547911a55927d8f7c9b4885.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that the other two nets give us pyramids. Therefore,  the correct answer is I.",
